Collection and Use of Your Data

Types of Data Collected:
The Company does not collect any of your personal data or other information that could identify you.

Data Storage

The Application does not store personal or other data, except for service-related information required for its functionality.

Router links added by the user within the Mikread application are stored in the internal folder of the application on your device in an encrypted form.
This data is not transmitted to the Company’s servers and does not leave your device.

You may delete stored links at any time through the application interface (in the connection management section).

Security of Data Transmission When Connecting to a Router

When using the Mikread app to connect to the router over the internet, the standard MikroTik API (port 8728) or REST API (www-ssl port) is used.
Data transmitted via the API, including the login and password for connection, is unencrypted.
The Company does not transmit or store this data on its servers and has no access to it. However, the User should be aware that when using an unencrypted connection, there is a risk that third parties may intercept this data.

It is recommended to use the application within local networks.

Data Deletion

All stored links and local data can be completely deleted by the user manually through the application interface or by uninstalling the application from the device.

